    Categories         All posts      Awards      Community      Design      Development      Documentation      Education      Events      Features      General      Interviews      Meta      Month in WordPress      Performance      Podcast      Releases      Security      Store      Testing      Updates      WordCamp      \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t  \n \n\n \n\n \n \n\t\n\t \n\t\t\n\t\t \n\t\t\t  October 28, 2026  \n\t\t\tBy   Aaron Jorbin  \n\t\t\tin   Releases  ,   Security  \n\t\t \n\t\t\n\n\t\t WordPress 7.1.4 \n\t \n\t\n\n\t\n\t \n\t\n\n\t\n\t \n\t\t \n This security release features fixes for multiple issues. \n\n\n\n  Because this is a security release, it is recommended that you update your sites immediately.  \n\n\n\n You can  download WordPress 7.1.4 from WordPress.org , or visit your WordPress Dashboard, click “Updates”, and then click “Update Now”. If you have sites that support automatic background updates, the update process will begin automatically. WordPress 7.1.4 is a short-cycle release. The next major release will be  version 7.2 , currently planned for December 8th. \n\n\n\n For more information, please visit the  WordPress 7.1.4 HelpHub site . \n\n\n\n Security updates included in this release \n\n\n\n The security team would like to thank the following people and organizations for responsibly reporting vulnerabilities, and allowing them to be fixed in this release: \n\n\n\n \n A weakness in the WordPress upgrade process which can lead to remote code execution during the upgrade window, reported by  Umut Bayram . \n\n\n\n A stored XSS with specially crafted block markup, reported by  Rafie Muhammad  (Awesome Motive, Inc.). \n\n\n\n Privacy Data Removal Requests can be created in a way that leads to stored XSS, reported by Anthropic. \n\n\n\n Multiple stored XSS issues in the Interactivity API independently discovered by AnC and DatNLQ from VietSunshine Cyber Security, rekter0 and Anas cherni,  Marcel Karlsson (whoismarcel) , and Weston Ruter, Jon Surrell, Alex Concha, and Luis Herranz of the WordPress Security Team. \n\n\n\n A stored denial of service issue in the Interactivity API, reported by Jon Surrell of the WordPress Security Team. \n\n\n\n A stored XSS in Customizer selective refresh, reported by  Rafie Muhammad  (Awesome Motive, Inc.). \n\n\n\n A Stored XSS in the Categories block reported by Ben Bidner of the WordPress Security Team. \n\n\n\n Specially crafted User Logins can lead to a stored XSS reported by Anthropic. \n\n\n\n Unpublished customizer changesets can be discovered by unauthenticated users, reported by  Antonio Lorensius Silaban . \n\n\n\n A Stored XSS in Playlist and image blocks, reported by Ben Bidner of the WordPress Security Team. \n\n\n\n Stored XSS in  core/comments-pagination-next  and  core/comments-pagination-previous  blocks, reported by Alex Concha of the WordPress Security Team. \n\n\n\n Notes can be read by privileged users that lack access to edit the post the note is attached to, reported by Ramon of the WordPress Security Team. \n\n\n\n An update to the bundled root certificates due to the eMudhra revocation. \n \n\n\n\n Thank you to these WordPress contributors \n\n\n\n This release was led by  Aaron Jorbin  and  Nik Tsekouras . WordPress 7.1.4 would not have been possible without the contributions of the following people: \n\n\n\n  Aaron Jorbin ,  Adam Silverstein ,  Alex Concha ,  Andrew Duthie ,  Andrew Serong ,  David Arenas ,  Dennis Snell ,  Ella Van Durpe ,  George Mamadashvili ,  Isabel Brison ,  Jake Spurlock ,  Jb Audras ,  Jeremy Felt ,  John Blackbourn ,  Jon Surrell ,  Jonathan Desrosiers ,  Kira Song,  Lance Willett ,  luisherranz ,  Marco Ciampini ,  marcs0h ,  Marin Atanasov ,  Mario Santos ,  Miguel Fonseca ,  Nik Tsekouras ,  Peter Wilson ,  ramonopoly ,  Rudy Faile ,  Sergey Biryukov ,  umut3806 ,  Weston Ruter  \n\n\n\n Backports \n\n\n\n As a courtesy, the security fixes were backported to all branches eligible to receive security fixes (currently through 4.7). As a reminder,  only the most recent version of WordPress is actively supported . The backports are in progress and will ship as they become ready. \n\n\n\n WordPress 7.2 Beta 3 has also been released, containing all applicable fixes. \n \n\n\t\t\n\t\t \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t Share this: \n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t   Share on Threads (Opens in new window)   Threads   \n\n\t\t\t\t\t   Share on Mastodon (Opens in new window)   Mastodon   \n\n\t\t\t\t\t   Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)   Bluesky   \n\n\t\t\t\t\t   Share on X (Opens in new window)   X   \n\n\t\t\t\t\t   Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)   Facebook   \n\n\t\t\t\t\t   Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)   LinkedIn   \n\n\t\t\t\t\t   Share using Native tools   Share  Copied to clipboard   \n\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\n\t\t \n\t\t\n\n\t \n\t\n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n \n\t   Previous   WordPress 7.2 Beta 2    \n\t   Next   WordPress 7.2 Beta 4   \n \n \n\n \n \n\t\n\t Get the latest updates \n\t\n\n\t\n\t \n\t\t\n\t\t \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t Subscribe to WordPress News \n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t \n\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tEmail Address\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t   \t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tSubscribe\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\tJoin 21.5K other subscribers\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t \n\t\n\t\t \n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t Contribute to WordPress \n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t WordPress is open-source software created by a global community. There are many ways to  get involved , whether through code, design, documentation, and more. \n\t\t\t\n\t\t \n\t\t\n\t \n\t\n \n\n \n