 ago       |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  Thank god we moved to Bruno and sometimes just http files in vs code or jetbrains      reply                             skilning    9 hours ago       |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  Enshittification wins again. :(      reply                             jongjong    6 hours ago       |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  How are people still using Postman? You can vibecode Postman in like 30 minutes. Do you even need it at all now? You can just ask the AI to write you a test suite in 5 minutes which calls all your endpoints with all the parameters and assertions you could possibly want. It's way more flexible than Postman and it's just a text file/script; you can share with any team member.      reply                             ern    1 hour ago       |  parent  |  next   [–]       \n  Yep, you can create a pretty HTML harness even for your APIs.      reply                             dsschnau    8 hours ago       |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  I'm glad to find out from this comment section that I'm not the only one who has noticed Postman is the poster-child of Enshittification.      reply                             Surac    10 hours ago       |  prev   [–]       \n  who the hell needs that. skills are just md files      reply                             fifilura    10 hours ago       |  parent   [–]       \n  Or pre-AI it was a python script inside a notebook.      reply             \n            \n   Guidelines  |  FAQ  |  Lists  |  API  |  Security  |  Legal  |  Apply to YC  |  Contact    \n Search:           "
