  "text": "        US002788                   US002788                menu    close    home     Certify a project    Get Started   Requirements   Certification Mark   License Agreement      The Certification Process    Introduction   Hardware   Software   Documentation   Branding      Projects    Project Listing   API      Open Source Hardware Basics    Frequently Asked Questions   About   OSHWA            Stringman    Nathaniel Nifong   mail         OSHWA UID  US002788   Project Website  Certification Date  November 07, 2025  Country  United States of America   Stringman is an overhead cable driven paralell robot for a single room. It is both a hardware design, and a collection of associated software. It can be assembled from 3d printed and purchased parts and controlled with either a gamepad or the LeRobot AI library The license on everything is Apache-2.0   Version  pilot       Licenses      Hardware  Other    Software  Other    Documentation  Other  View Documentation       Certification mark      SVG   PNG      SVG   PNG      The  OSHW Certification Mark  shows the project's unique certification ID and makes it easy for users to quickly find this page along with the project's details. This mark can be used throughout the project's design, documentation, and promotional material.  For more details, take a look at the  Certification Mark Usage Guide .         Project Type   Robotics  3D Printing  Education  Electronics       Keywords  robot, cdpr, gripper, lerobot, teleoperation, household          Certify a Project   The Certification Process   Certified Projects   Basics   Frequently Asked Questions   About   OSHWA   Privacy Policy             With support from                       This work is licensed under a  Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License .            "
